**Theorem 4.3 (matched inherited-representation comparison).** Instantiate
the inherited five-occurrence switch representation on these same 74
roles, the same optional finite slots and the same native occurrence
word, with the identical role/route lists. Denote it by subscript 5.
Then

$$
\begin{aligned}
V_5&=147+2q+4c+48C,&L_5&=74+q+2c+24C,\\
V_5-V_U&=3c+24C,&L_5-L_U&=2c+16C.
\end{aligned}
$$

Writing $m_i=|\mathcal D_i|$, its matched stencil satisfies

$$
g_{5,i}-g_i
 =9c_{i-1}+72m_i+t_i+192e_i+24s_i.
$$

The two actual storage images are mutually decodable and preserve native
rows under their own rules. Whole-price superiority holds under this
comparison exactly when the extra fixed apparatus price $\rho_U-\rho_5$
is smaller than the summed foundation/stencil saving; no such apparatus
price ordering is asserted.

Proof. The inherited cell has 47 vertices and 24 terminals; its tape
increment is 48. Its present optional bit adds four vertices and two
terminals to its socket. Summing with $F_{75}$ proves the re-counted
formulas. Both representations decode to the same raw record, so
encoding after the other decoder gives inverse maps on their actual
images. Using Definition 2.3's actual raw-pattern enumeration with the
inherited four-assignment switch and 48-vertex append templates gives
its own row square by the same opcode/effect cases as Theorem 2.4.
Thus their row squares transport the same native edges; the old
canonical-control theorem is not being broadened without this instance.
This is not an installed migration between two live machines.

Inherited cell inspection costs 140 and finite inspection
$6q+12c-4$. All root/head/append routes stop at the same native roots,
so their lengths agree. Probe saving is $9c+72m_i$; old-bit assignment
saving is $t_i$. Inherited births are $48e_i+4s_i$ rather than
$24e_i+s_i$. Their vertex-plus-initialization difference is
$8(24e_i+3s_i)=192e_i+24s_i$. Old-root assignments and head terms
agree. This proves the row difference. Foundation saving is
$8(V_{5,0}-V_{U,0})=384+24c_0$ under the same convention. Add the
actual fixed apparatus difference to obtain the stated necessary and
sufficient inequality for that scalar price comparison. A packed-byte
alternative changes both its cell-rewrite stencil and finite rules;
fewer vertices alone do not compare its whole run with this one. ∎

